{
  "description": "Tick-normalized height-mode time-lock vectors: nLockTime, nSequence, and coinbase maturity. T(x) is the cumulative tick of block x, inclusive of its own interval, from the schedule. Height-mode predicates: nLockTime is strict and absolute — final in block b iff T(b) > 600*lockTime; nSequence is weak and relative — mature in block b iff T(b) - T(fundingBlock) >= 600*relativeLock; coinbase maturity is weak and absolute — spendable in block b iff T(b) - T(creationBlock) >= 60,000. Mempool forms use T(tip+1) from the schedule, never T(tip)+tau(tip). BCHN escape clauses: nLockTime==0 is final everywhere; every-input-SEQUENCE_FINAL is final regardless of nLockTime. A coinbase transaction is exempt from both predicates: it is always final, whatever its nLockTime and whatever the nSequence of its single input (CHIP: Coinbase Exemption). The exemption is a scope restriction on the predicates, so it lives in the caller and the evaluators are coinbase-agnostic; the lock_coinbase_* vectors model that short circuit via `subjectIsCoinbase`, and lock_noncoinbase_bip54_twin pins that an identical non-coinbase is still bound. Coinbase maturity is unaffected, because it reads the spent output's height and a coinbase spends none. MTP-mode comparison and the LOCKTIME_THRESHOLD split are unchanged and out of scope. Every expected value is a hand-derived golden pin; the generator verifies the shared reference evaluators (timelock_ticks.h) against the pins and refuses to emit on any mismatch. All integer values are decimal strings to preserve full 64-bit precision.",
